        "title": "Feature health split from runtime evidence in status probes",
        "summary": "Observability now distinguishes user-facing feature health from the specific runtime (production-api, desktop-release, local-dev) that produced each piece of evidence.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Status checks now declare a runtime environment alongside the feature they prove, so the dashboard can label rows by runtime and treat production-auth media probes as informational while desktop-release remains the source of truth for Media Generation.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "6b9c8b0786777e2fbb7442179a1f5253a441fbd9"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Reworked status policy, investigator, repairer, and StatusView to group checks by feature and reflect the new feature/runtime split, with refreshed docs in aura-feature-health.md and added policy tests.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "6b9c8b0786777e2fbb7442179a1f5253a441fbd9"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Release-nightly and release-stable desktop legs now also probe image-generation-stream, extending the desktop-release coverage beyond auth, orgs, and local agents.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "6b9c8b0786777e2fbb7442179a1f5253a441fbd9"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-2",
        "time_label": "9:52 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-06-15T16:52:53.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-06-15T16:52:53.000Z",
        "title": "Analytics rebuilt for accurate True DAU with a CI contract gate",
        "summary": "A new typed event registry, server-only session_active emitter, and build-time guards make analytics a hard release requirement across web, desktop, iOS, and Android.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Introduced a typed analytics registry plus AST/pipeline/server contract tests so renaming, dropping, or non-literal track() calls fail loudly instead of silently breaking metrics.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "57b077e8e3596117c08ce0ae032de9bd8e60386c"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Moved session_active to a single server-side emitter and updated the Mixpanel server module to enforce the single-emitter and manifest invariants via cargo tests.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "57b077e8e3596117c08ce0ae032de9bd8e60386c"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "iOS and Android fastlane release lanes now require VITE_MIXPANEL_TOKEN and run --require-analytics validation, so TestFlight and Play Store builds can no longer ship with a no-op browser SDK.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "57b077e8e3596117c08ce0ae032de9bd8e60386c"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Added a dedicated Analytics Contract GitHub workflow that runs on every push to main and PR touching the interface or server, gating regressions on both client and server analytics.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "57b077e8e3596117c08ce0ae032de9bd8e60386c"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-3",
        "time_label": "12:40 PM",
        "started_at": "2026-06-15T19:40:29.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-06-15T20:04:18.000Z",
        "title": "Dirty frontend builds blocked and probe coverage broadens to notes and public content",
        "summary": "Vite now refuses to produce analytics-enabled bundles with empty, 0.0.0, or -dirty versions, while feature-health probes pick up notes, processes, billing transactions, and public content details.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Vite analytics-enabled builds and the desktop-frontend-assets validator now reject APP_VERSION values that are empty, 0.0.0, or end in -dirty, closing the gap where a mis-versioned web bundle could ship past the previous release guard.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "5d7fff8c58ed75b527e47b87750c36fcfe3fd391"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Greatly expanded feature-health probe coverage with a 552-line addition to run-status-probes.mjs and new expectations for org-tool-actions-contract, billing-account-transactions, notes-crud, public-content-details, and analytics-contract-artifacts.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "d58f85fb70f60c2b71dc12cf9427d8adba4efb51"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Desktop release probes now exercise desktop-update-runtime, project-agent-chat-stream, session-share public reads, harness memory/skills roundtrips, notes CRUD, and a full process-run lifecycle, materially deepening what each desktop release leg verifies.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "d58f85fb70f60c2b71dc12cf9427d8adba4efb51"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Notes API now accepts the frontend's camelCase folderId, backed by a serde test, fixing a quiet contract mismatch the new notes-crud probe would otherwise surface.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "d58f85fb70f60c2b71dc12cf9427d8adba4efb51"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
